# Vairiot backups — install on the prod host with:
#   crontab -l | cat - /opt/Vairiot/infra/backup.crontab | crontab -
# or edit `crontab -e` and paste the lines below.
#
# All settings come from /opt/Vairiot/.env (see DEPLOY.md → Backups):
#   BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENT, BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT, BACKUP_S3_BUCKET,
#   BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY, BACKUP_S3_SECRET_KEY (EU region for GDPR).
# Nothing secret belongs in this file. (It used to pass a placeholder age key
# here, which made encryption fail and left an unencrypted archive behind.)
#
# A failed or incomplete run writes a [BACKUP-FAILED] / [BACKUP-INCOMPLETE]
# line to the log and exits non-zero; alert on either.

# Daily backup at 02:30 UTC: 30 daily + 12 monthly copies off-host.
30 2 * * * bash /opt/Vairiot/infra/backup.sh >> /var/log/vairiot-backup.log 2>&1

# Monthly restore test on the 2nd at 04:00 UTC: restores the newest off-host
# backup into a throwaway stack and checks it. Needs the age *private* key on
# this host (BACKUP_AGE_IDENTITY in .env); if you keep that key elsewhere, run
# the test from that machine instead and leave this line commented out.
# 0 4 2 * * bash /opt/Vairiot/infra/restore-test.sh >> /var/log/vairiot-restore-test.log 2>&1
